# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Per-machine Supabase target. .env.production is committed on purpose (the
# anon key is publishable); .env.development.local points at your own dev
# project and is yours alone. Covered by *.local above — spelled out because
# the difference between these two files is the difference between editing
# test data and editing the real logbook.
.env*.local

# Claude Code: shared project config is committed (CLAUDE.md,
# .claude/settings.json); per-machine overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Skills installed by the plugin manager — 282 files of somebody else's
# documentation, two copies of it, and not this project's to carry. The
# lockfile beside them *is* committed: it names the source and the hash, so the
# content is reinstallable and the version is recorded. Vendoring the pages
# themselves would mean hand-carrying their updates forever.
#
# `.agents/` is where the installer put them; `.claude/skills/` is the copy
# Claude Code actually reads. Neither is lintable — 141 markdown files and no
# JavaScript — so this is about the repository's history, not about the build.
.agents/
.claude/skills/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
